      "evidence": "design.md decision 3 says \"any internal error also denies with its message (fail closed only inside a managed task)\", and the spec says writes outside an active managed task \"SHALL NOT be affected\". In template/scripts/model_routing.py `_write_gate_main`, the invalid-JSON, missing-`file_path`, missing-`cwd` and no-existing-ancestor branches all return `deny(...)` before any managed-task check. The broad `except Exception` around the `git rev-parse` call and `check_task_write` also denies. A malformed payload or a git or OS error in an unrelated repository would therefore block a write the spec says is unaffected. The only tested outside-repo case is a well-formed payload, which is allowed.",
